Subject: [PATCH 3/5] feat(mem_cache): elastic VMM expert row arenas, lazy KV,
 quantized QSA pools

Port the placement/elastic, lazy-VMM KV and quantized QSA KV subsystems onto
main b02e16a895.

- row_arena.py / expert_elastic.py: CUDA VMM row arenas in routing-mass rank
  order, fixed row addresses across shrink/regrow, and the elastic expert
  cache with a live S control file (SGLANG_MOE_ELASTIC_CTL).
- kv_vmm_backing.py: ensure_prefix / uncommit_beyond / release_beyond /
  backed_tokens / bytes_per_token adapted to main's BumpArenaStub and
  VmmReservation; imports moved to sglang.srt.utils.cuda_vmm_utils.
- allocator/paged.py + allocator/token.py + kv_cache_configurator.py: lazy
  commit hooks, idle release, virtual capacity SGLANG_KV_LAZY_TOKENS and the
  min(requested, SAFETY x profiled) admission cap.
- memory_pool.py: lazy_ensure / lazy_release with the driver-free watermark
  and expert-cache shrink-first behaviour, plus tiered ring and scale/smooth
  accessors on HybridLinearKVPool.
- int8_g64 / int4_g32 / int8ring_int4 pools and their dequant-on-gather read
  and quantize-on-write kernels in sparse_attn.py / qwen_sparse_attn_backend.py;
  kv_cache_dtype mapping and the arg_groups KV choices.

Dropped the measurement-only kv_stats / kv_fakeq hooks. The
SGLANG_QSA_PREFILL_HOST_LENS experiment stays off.

Known reconciliation item for the kernel-correctness gate: main's trtllm
paged decode path passes zero_fill_cols=stride (padded-row zero fill); the
quantized gather branches currently pack compact rows and do not yet zero the
padded tails.
